build/
*.o
*.d
*.elf
*.bin
*.map
.DS_Store

# Except the released images, which are the point of that directory: an
# image somebody can download and run without a toolchain.
!builds/*.elf

tools/__pycache__/
build/kosmos.img

# The disk `run-kosmos.sh` makes beside whatever image it was given.
#
# That is right for a released binary - a downloader gets a disk without
# being told to make one - and wrong here, because running it against an
# ELF at the repository root leaves a 64 MB file in the working tree that
# `git add -A` will happily commit. Which is exactly what happened in
# 6157897, and GitHub said so on the next two pushes.
/kosmos.img

# The knowledge graph the `/graphify` skill builds from this tree.
#
# It was tracked - 284 files and 8.9 MB of caches, reports and JSON - which
# is a derived artefact of the source committed beside the source. It is
# rebuilt by running the skill again, and it changes on every run, so every
# run made a diff.
graphify-out/
